@startuml
title One transmit queue, so frames never interleave

rectangle "handler A" as A
rectangle "handler B" as B
rectangle "event source" as E
rectangle "timeout task" as T
queue "TX queue" as Q
rectangle "encoder" as Enc
rectangle "transport.write()" as W

A --> Q
B --> Q
E --> Q
T --> Q
Q --> Enc
Enc --> W

note bottom of Q
  Every producer goes through the same queue:
  two tasks writing at once would corrupt a frame.
end note
@enduml
